IMPORT prelude

-- Telecommunications Act 1997 (Cth), Schedule 3 (carriers' powers and immunities), Parts 1 and 3, and s 591 -- baseline
-- encoding from the seat of the owner or occupier of land a carrier enters, inspects, builds on or maintains: must I be
-- told first, and how far ahead (cl 17); can the carrier cut my trees (cl 18); how long can a temporary tower stay (cl 8A,
-- 8B, 8C); by when must my land be restored (cl 9, 9A); can I claim compensation for loss or damage, and in which court
-- (cl 42, 43, 46(7)); can I claim if my property is in effect acquired (cl 62, 63; s 591); is the facility mine, and must I
-- pay if I subdivide (cl 47, 53).
--
-- SEAT: the landholder -- the owner of the land, or an occupier other than the owner. "Must the carrier tell me before it
-- comes onto my land? Can it cut down my trees? When must it put my land back? Can I get compensation, and where do I sue?"
-- Schedule 3 is addressed to carriers; their duties are encoded as what they mean for the landholder. No question is asked
-- from the seat of the carrier, the ACMA or the Minister.
--
-- EDITION: the compilation registered as C2026C00224 (Compilation No. 117, compilation date 4 June 2026), retrieved from the
-- Federal Register of Legislation on 13 October 2026, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05145.txt (Schedule 3
-- Part 1 at lines 15102-15885, Part 3 at 15905-15928, s 591 at 14059). No instrument is deposited: the low-impact facilities
-- determination (cl 6(3)), the regulations (cl 3, 7(5)(d), 14) and the Ministerial Code of Practice (cl 15) are inputs or
-- out of scope.
--
-- CLOCKS. Notice, tree-request and restoration periods are counted in business days, as the person counts them; the
-- removal period and the calendar-year limits in days. Schedule 3 does not define "business day" (the Act defines it only
-- section by section, as in s 55(3)), so the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B meaning (borrowed, not deposited) would
-- apply: not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday in the place concerned. The person's own count is the input.
--
-- Every judgment the text leaves to the carrier or a court (whether the work "need[s] to be carried out without delay",
-- whether the carrier "considers" notice impracticable, the "reasonable amount" of compensation, whether there is an
-- "acquisition of property" in the constitutional sense) is asked as a fact. Nothing is decided for them.

§ `Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3 -- the owner or occupier of land a carrier works on`

§§ `The parties and their acts`

-- The parties Schedule 3 names, as they meet the landholder. Clause 43 extends the carrier's powers to its employees, its
-- contractors and their employees; they act as "the carrier" here.
DECLARE `Land party` IS ONE OF
    `the carrier`
    `me, the landholder`

DECLARE `Land act` IS ONE OF
    -- cl 17(1): "give written notice of its intention to do so"
    `give me written notice of the activity`
    -- cl 17(4): "before the carrier begins to engage in the activity"
    `begin the activity on my land`
    -- cl 18(1): the request "that the tree be cut down or lopped, or that the undergrowth or vegetation be cleared ... in the
    -- manner, and within the period, specified in the notice"
    `cut down, lop or clear as the carrier requested`
    -- cl 18(2): "The carrier may only engage in those activities if the request is not complied with."
    `cut down, lop or clear the trees or vegetation itself`
    -- cl 8A: "the carrier must remove the facility within 28 days after ..."
    `remove the temporary facility`
    -- cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4): "take all reasonable steps to ensure that the restoration begins within 10 business days"
    `begin restoring my land`

-- Whether a rule, run over a list of events, ends FULFILLED. (A breached or still-open rule cannot be compared with EQUALS
-- on the stable l4, so the questions below that run a rule ask this.)
GIVEN d IS A DEONTIC `Land party` `Land act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the rule ends fulfilled` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `What the carrier is doing (Divisions 2, 3 and 4)`

-- Schedule 3 Part 1 gives a carrier three powers over land: to inspect it (Division 2, cl 5), to install a facility
-- (Division 3, cl 6) and to maintain a facility (Division 4, cl 7). The conditions in Division 5 (cl 8-20) and the
-- compensation in cl 42 attach only to "an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4". Work a carrier does by agreement, or under a
-- State planning approval, is outside them.
DECLARE `Carrier activity` IS ONE OF
    `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)`
    `installing a facility (Division 3)`
    `maintaining a facility (Division 4)`
    `something not done under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3`

GIVEN activity IS A `Carrier activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4` IF
    CONSIDER activity
    WHEN `something not done under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- cl 17(1)(a), (b), cl 18(1)(c), (d): notice goes to "the owner of the land; and if the land is occupied by a person other
-- than the owner--the occupier".
GIVEN `I own the land` IS A BOOLEAN, `I occupy the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am owed the notice as owner or occupier` IF
        `I own the land`
    OR  `I occupy the land`

-- cl 17(6), 18(4), 19(3): the urgent-work exception -- "those activities need to be carried out without delay in order to
-- protect: (i) the integrity of a telecommunications network or a facility; or (ii) the health or safety of persons; or
-- (iii) the environment; or (iv) property; or (v) the maintenance of an adequate level of service." Asked as one fact.

-- cl 17(4A)(a)-(d), (7)(a)-(d): an inspection that "(a) is not inconsistent with Australia's obligations under a listed
-- international agreement; and (b) could not have an effect described in one or more of subparagraphs 27(7)(a)(ii) to (xii)
-- ... ; and (c) will not have an adverse effect on a streetscape or other landscape; and (d) will not have an impact on a
-- place, area or thing described in paragraph 27(7)(c) or (d)". Called here a "low-effect inspection" (not the Act's term).
GIVEN `consistent with listed international agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `could have none of the cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) effects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no adverse effect on a streetscape or landscape` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no impact on a cl 27(7)(c) or (d) place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inspection is low-effect` IF
        `consistent with listed international agreements`
    AND `could have none of the cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) effects`
    AND `no adverse effect on a streetscape or landscape`
    AND `no impact on a cl 27(7)(c) or (d) place`

§§ `cl 17 -- must the carrier tell me before it comes onto my land, and how far ahead`

-- cl 17(4): "The notice must be given at least 10 business days before the carrier begins to engage in the activity."
-- cl 17(4A): "Despite subclause (4), the notice need be given only 2 business days before the carrier begins to engage in an
-- activity authorised by Division 2 (which deals with inspection) that:" meets (a)-(d).
`the business days of notice before work` MEANS 10
`the business days of notice before a low-effect inspection` MEANS 2

DECLARE `Notice owed to me` IS ONE OF
    `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
    `yes: written notice at least 2 business days before the carrier begins this inspection, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(3), (4A))`
    `no: I am neither the owner nor an occupier, so cl 17 gives me no notice (cl 17(1))`
    `no: I waived my right to the notice (cl 17(5))`
    `no: the work must be done without delay to protect a network or facility, people's health or safety, the environment, property or an adequate level of service (cl 17(6))`
    `no: the work concerns a temporary defence facility and the carrier considers notice impracticable (cl 17(6A))`
    `no: it is an inspection of land that is a public place, with none of the listed effects (cl 17(7))`
    `no: it is the installation of a temporary low-impact facility for emergency services (cl 17(8), cl 6(5)(g))`
    `not covered: cl 17 applies only to an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3`

GIVEN activity IS A `Carrier activity`
      `I own the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I occupy the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I waived the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work must be done without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it concerns a temporary defence facility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the carrier considers notice impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land is a public place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `consistent with listed international agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `could have none of the cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) effects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no adverse effect on a streetscape or landscape` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no impact on a cl 27(7)(c) or (d) place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a temporary tower for emergency services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice owed to me`
DECIDE `the notice owed to me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`it is an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4` activity))
        THEN `not covered: cl 17 applies only to an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3`
        IF (NOT (`I am owed the notice as owner or occupier` `I own the land` `I occupy the land`))
        THEN `no: I am neither the owner nor an occupier, so cl 17 gives me no notice (cl 17(1))`
        IF `I waived the notice`
        THEN `no: I waived my right to the notice (cl 17(5))`
        IF `the work must be done without delay`
        THEN `no: the work must be done without delay to protect a network or facility, people's health or safety, the environment, property or an adequate level of service (cl 17(6))`
        IF `it concerns a temporary defence facility` AND `the carrier considers notice impracticable`
        THEN `no: the work concerns a temporary defence facility and the carrier considers notice impracticable (cl 17(6A))`
        IF `low-effect` AND `is inspection` AND `the land is a public place`
        THEN `no: it is an inspection of land that is a public place, with none of the listed effects (cl 17(7))`
        IF activity EQUALS `installing a facility (Division 3)` AND `it is a temporary tower for emergency services`
        THEN `no: it is the installation of a temporary low-impact facility for emergency services (cl 17(8), cl 6(5)(g))`
        IF `low-effect` AND `is inspection`
        THEN `yes: written notice at least 2 business days before the carrier begins this inspection, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(3), (4A))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
    WHERE
        `is inspection` MEANS activity EQUALS `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)`
        `low-effect` MEANS `the inspection is low-effect` `consistent with listed international agreements` `could have none of the cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) effects` `no adverse effect on a streetscape or landscape` `no impact on a cl 27(7)(c) or (d) place`

@export Must a carrier (a telecommunications company) give me written notice before it inspects my land, installs a facility on it or maintains one, and how far ahead (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 17)?
GIVEN activity IS A `Carrier activity` @desc What the carrier is doing on the land: inspecting or surveying it (Division 2), installing a facility such as a cable, pit or tower (Division 3), maintaining an existing facility (Division 4), or something done under an agreement or a State approval instead
      `I own the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the land
      `I occupy the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you occupy the land without owning it (for example as a tenant)
      `I waived the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have waived your right to be given the notice
      `the work must be done without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work needs to be done without delay to protect the network or a facility, people's health or safety, the environment, property, or an adequate level of service
      `it concerns a temporary defence facility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work concerns a temporary facility for use by or for a defence organisation for defence purposes
      `the carrier considers notice impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the carrier considers giving the notice impracticable in the circumstances
      `the land is a public place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is a public place (a place to which members of the public have ready access)
      `consistent with listed international agreements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an inspection: whether it is consistent with Australia's obligations under the international agreements listed in the regulations
      `could have none of the cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) effects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an inspection: whether it could have none of the environmental effects listed in Schedule 3, cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) (such as on threatened species, heritage or Aboriginal places)
      `no adverse effect on a streetscape or landscape` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an inspection: whether it will have no adverse effect on a streetscape or other landscape
      `no impact on a cl 27(7)(c) or (d) place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an inspection: whether it will have no impact on a place, area or thing described in Schedule 3, cl 27(7)(c) or (d)
      `it is a temporary tower for emergency services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an installation: whether it is a temporary low-impact tower installed to give emergency services capacity in an emergency or natural disaster
GIVETH A `Notice owed to me`
DECIDE `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` IS
    `the notice owed to me` activity `I own the land` `I occupy the land` `I waived the notice` `the work must be done without delay` `it concerns a temporary defence facility` `the carrier considers notice impracticable` `the land is a public place` `consistent with listed international agreements` `could have none of the cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) effects` `no adverse effect on a streetscape or landscape` `no impact on a cl 27(7)(c) or (d) place` `it is a temporary tower for emergency services`

-- cl 17(2), (3), (4), (4A): what a notice that was owed must contain, and when. The count is the number of business days
-- from the day the notice was given to the day the work began (the work beginning on the nth business day after the notice
-- day counts n). Read so, "at least 10 business days before" is met at n = 10. A clear-days reading would need 11: see
-- NOTES.md, finding 3.
GIVEN activity IS A `Carrier activity`
      `low-effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the business days of notice required` IS
    BRANCH
        IF activity EQUALS `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` AND `low-effect`
        THEN `the business days of notice before a low-effect inspection`
        OTHERWISE `the business days of notice before work`

DECLARE `Notice check` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the notice stated the purpose and the compensation statement and was given early enough (cl 17(2)-(4))`
    `no: the notice did not specify the purpose of the activity (cl 17(2))`
    `no: the notice did not state that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(3))`
    `no: the notice was given too late (cl 17(4), (4A))`
    `not covered: cl 17 applies only to an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3`

@export If I was owed notice under cl 17, did the carrier's notice say what it must and come early enough (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 17(2)-(4A))?
GIVEN activity IS A `Carrier activity` @desc What the carrier is doing on the land: inspecting or surveying it (Division 2), installing a facility (Division 3), maintaining a facility (Division 4), or something else
      `the notice specified the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the written notice said for what purpose the carrier intended to do the work
      `the notice stated compensation may be payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice said that compensation may be payable under clause 42 if a person suffers financial loss or damage to property because of the work
      `business days from notice to work` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting business days (not weekends or public holidays) from the day you were given the notice, on which business day after it did the carrier begin? (Begun on the 10th business day after the notice day: enter 10)
      `consistent with listed international agreements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an inspection: whether it is consistent with Australia's obligations under the international agreements listed in the regulations
      `could have none of the cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) effects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an inspection: whether it could have none of the environmental effects listed in Schedule 3, cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii)
      `no adverse effect on a streetscape or landscape` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an inspection: whether it will have no adverse effect on a streetscape or other landscape
      `no impact on a cl 27(7)(c) or (d) place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an inspection: whether it will have no impact on a place, area or thing described in Schedule 3, cl 27(7)(c) or (d)
GIVETH A `Notice check`
DECIDE `Was the notice I was given good enough` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`it is an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4` activity))
        THEN `not covered: cl 17 applies only to an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3`
        IF (NOT `the notice specified the purpose`)
        THEN `no: the notice did not specify the purpose of the activity (cl 17(2))`
        IF (NOT `the notice stated compensation may be payable`)
        THEN `no: the notice did not state that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(3))`
        IF (NOT (`the rule ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`cl 17(4), (4A) -- the carrier must not begin before the notice period has run` (`the business days of notice required` activity `low-effect`)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `begin the activity on my land` `business days from notice to work`)))))
        THEN `no: the notice was given too late (cl 17(4), (4A))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the notice stated the purpose and the compensation statement and was given early enough (cl 17(2)-(4))`
    WHERE
        `low-effect` MEANS `the inspection is low-effect` `consistent with listed international agreements` `could have none of the cl 27(7)(a)(ii)-(xii) effects` `no adverse effect on a streetscape or landscape` `no impact on a cl 27(7)(c) or (d) place`

-- The same timing as a prohibition on the carrier, on a business-day clock starting on the day the notice is given: it
-- must not begin before the nth business day, n being the period. (WITHIN is inclusive, so the window of prohibition is
-- one less than the period.)
GIVEN `the period of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land party` `Land act`
DECIDE `cl 17(4), (4A) -- the carrier must not begin before the notice period has run` IS
    PARTY `the carrier`
    SHANT `begin the activity on my land`
    WITHIN (`the period of notice` MINUS 1)
    LEST  BREACH BY `the carrier` BECAUSE "cl 17(4), (4A): the notice must be given at least 10 business days (2 for a low-effect inspection) before the carrier begins"

§§ `cl 18 -- can the carrier cut down or lop my trees, or clear vegetation`

-- cl 18(1): "At least 10 business days before engaging in any of the following activities under Division 2, 3 or 4: (a)
-- cutting down or lopping a tree on private land; (b) clearing or removing undergrowth or vegetation on private land; a
-- carrier must give: (c) the owner of the land; and (d) if the land is occupied by a person other than the owner--the
-- occupier; a written notice requesting that the tree be cut down or lopped, or that the undergrowth or vegetation be
-- cleared, as the case may be, in the manner, and within the period, specified in the notice." (2): "The carrier may only
-- engage in those activities if the request is not complied with." (3) waiver; (3A) temporary defence facility; (4) urgent.
`the business days of a tree request before the work` MEANS 10

DECLARE `Tree answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I did not do the work the carrier's request asked for within the period it specified, so the carrier may do it itself (cl 18(2))`
    `no: I did what the carrier's request asked within the period it specified, so the carrier may not do it itself (cl 18(2))`
    `no: the carrier must first give me a written request, at least 10 business days before, asking me to do it myself in a stated manner and period (cl 18(1), (2))`
    `no: the carrier's request was not given at least 10 business days before the work (cl 18(1))`
    `cl 18 does not stand in the way: I waived my right to the request (cl 18(3))`
    `cl 18 does not stand in the way: the work must be done without delay to protect a network or facility, people's health or safety, the environment, property or an adequate level of service (cl 18(4))`
    `cl 18 does not stand in the way: the work concerns a temporary defence facility and the carrier considers the request impracticable (cl 18(3A))`
    `not covered: cl 18 applies only to trees, undergrowth or vegetation on private land, cut or cleared in an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4, and gives the request only to the owner and an occupier`

@export Can the carrier cut down or lop trees, or clear undergrowth or vegetation, on my land itself (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 18)?
GIVEN activity IS A `Carrier activity` @desc What the carrier is doing on the land: inspecting or surveying it (Division 2), installing a facility (Division 3), maintaining a facility (Division 4), or something else
      `the land is private land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trees or vegetation are on private land
      `I own the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the land
      `I occupy the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you occupy the land without owning it (for example as a tenant)
      `I waived the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have waived your right to be given the request
      `the work must be done without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work needs to be done without delay to protect the network or a facility, people's health or safety, the environment, property, or an adequate level of service
      `it concerns a temporary defence facility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work concerns a temporary facility for use by or for a defence organisation for defence purposes
      `the carrier considers the request impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the carrier considers giving the request impracticable in the circumstances
      `I was given a written request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the carrier gave you a written notice asking you to cut down or lop the tree, or clear the vegetation, yourself in a stated manner and period
      `business days from request to work` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting business days from the day you were given the request, on which business day after it does (or did) the carrier propose to do the work? (The 10th business day after: enter 10)
      `I did what the request asked within its period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cut down, lopped or cleared as the request asked, in its manner and within its period
GIVETH A `Tree answer`
DECIDE `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`it is an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4` activity)) OR (NOT `the land is private land`) OR (NOT (`I am owed the notice as owner or occupier` `I own the land` `I occupy the land`))
        THEN `not covered: cl 18 applies only to trees, undergrowth or vegetation on private land, cut or cleared in an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4, and gives the request only to the owner and an occupier`
        IF `I waived the request`
        THEN `cl 18 does not stand in the way: I waived my right to the request (cl 18(3))`
        IF `the work must be done without delay`
        THEN `cl 18 does not stand in the way: the work must be done without delay to protect a network or facility, people's health or safety, the environment, property or an adequate level of service (cl 18(4))`
        IF `it concerns a temporary defence facility` AND `the carrier considers the request impracticable`
        THEN `cl 18 does not stand in the way: the work concerns a temporary defence facility and the carrier considers the request impracticable (cl 18(3A))`
        IF (NOT `I was given a written request`)
        THEN `no: the carrier must first give me a written request, at least 10 business days before, asking me to do it myself in a stated manner and period (cl 18(1), (2))`
        IF `business days from request to work` LESS THAN `the business days of a tree request before the work`
        THEN `no: the carrier's request was not given at least 10 business days before the work (cl 18(1))`
        IF `I did what the request asked within its period`
        THEN `no: I did what the carrier's request asked within the period it specified, so the carrier may not do it itself (cl 18(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: I did not do the work the carrier's request asked for within the period it specified, so the carrier may do it itself (cl 18(2))`

-- The same as a rule over time, on a clock (in business days) starting when the request is given: the landholder may do the
-- work within the period the request specifies; only if that period passes without it may the carrier do it.
GIVEN `the period specified in the request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land party` `Land act`
DECIDE `cl 18(1), (2) -- I am asked to do it myself; only if I do not may the carrier` IS
    PARTY `me, the landholder`
    DO    `cut down, lop or clear as the carrier requested`
    WITHIN `the period specified in the request`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the carrier`
        MAY   `cut down, lop or clear the trees or vegetation itself`

§§ `cl 8A, 8B, 8C -- how long can a temporary facility stay on my land`

-- Temporary low-impact towers (cl 6(5)(b)-(g)) and temporary facilities installed in maintenance (cl 7(3A)). Whether a
-- facility is a low-impact facility turns on the Minister's determination under cl 6(3), not deposited: asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Temporary facility` IS ONE OF
    `a temporary tower while another facility is maintained (cl 6(5)(b))`
    `a temporary tower while another facility is replaced (cl 6(5)(c))`
    `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))`
    `a temporary tower for a series of events at a venue (cl 6(5)(e))`
    `a temporary tower for a high-demand holiday period (cl 6(5)(f))`
    `a temporary tower for emergency services in an emergency or natural disaster (cl 6(5)(g))`
    `a temporary facility while the original facility is maintained (cl 7(3A))`

-- cl 8A(1)-(6): "the carrier must remove the facility within 28 days after" the end of the maintenance, the replacement, the
-- event, the last of the events, the emergency need, or the maintenance.
`the days to remove a temporary facility` MEANS 28

DECLARE `Removal deadline` IS ONE OF
    `within 28 days after the maintenance of the other facility is completed (cl 8A(1))`
    `within 28 days after the replacement of the other facility is completed (cl 8A(2))`
    `within 28 days after the end of the event (cl 8A(3))`
    `within 28 days after the end of the last of the events (cl 8A(4))`
    `within 28 days after it ceases to be needed for emergency services to deal with the emergency or natural disaster (cl 8A(5))`
    `within 28 days after the maintenance of the original facility is completed (cl 8A(6))`
    `cl 8A sets no removal deadline for a holiday-period tower; it may stay at the place no more than 90 days in a calendar year (cl 8C)`

@export By when must the carrier remove a temporary tower or other temporary facility from my land (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 8A)?
GIVEN facility IS A `Temporary facility` @desc Which kind of temporary facility the carrier installed: a tower during maintenance or replacement of another facility, for an event or series of events at a venue, for a holiday period, for emergency services, or another temporary facility during maintenance
GIVETH A `Removal deadline`
DECIDE `By when must the temporary facility be removed` IS
    CONSIDER facility
    WHEN `a temporary tower while another facility is maintained (cl 6(5)(b))` THEN `within 28 days after the maintenance of the other facility is completed (cl 8A(1))`
    WHEN `a temporary tower while another facility is replaced (cl 6(5)(c))` THEN `within 28 days after the replacement of the other facility is completed (cl 8A(2))`
    WHEN `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` THEN `within 28 days after the end of the event (cl 8A(3))`
    WHEN `a temporary tower for a series of events at a venue (cl 6(5)(e))` THEN `within 28 days after the end of the last of the events (cl 8A(4))`
    WHEN `a temporary tower for emergency services in an emergency or natural disaster (cl 6(5)(g))` THEN `within 28 days after it ceases to be needed for emergency services to deal with the emergency or natural disaster (cl 8A(5))`
    WHEN `a temporary facility while the original facility is maintained (cl 7(3A))` THEN `within 28 days after the maintenance of the original facility is completed (cl 8A(6))`
    WHEN `a temporary tower for a high-demand holiday period (cl 6(5)(f))` THEN `cl 8A sets no removal deadline for a holiday-period tower; it may stay at the place no more than 90 days in a calendar year (cl 8C)`

-- The removal duty as a rule, in days from the event that starts the clock.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land party` `Land act`
DECIDE `cl 8A -- the carrier must remove the temporary facility within 28 days` IS
    PARTY `the carrier`
    MUST  `remove the temporary facility`
    WITHIN `the days to remove a temporary facility`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the carrier` BECAUSE "cl 8A: the carrier must remove the temporary facility within 28 days after the maintenance, replacement, event or emergency need ends"

DECLARE `Removal status` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the carrier removed the temporary facility within 28 days (cl 8A)`
    `late: the carrier did not remove the temporary facility within 28 days (cl 8A)`
    `not yet late: the 28 days have not run out (cl 8A)`
    `not covered: cl 8A sets no removal deadline for a holiday-period tower; see the calendar-year limit in cl 8C`

@export Did the carrier remove the temporary tower or other temporary facility from my land in time (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 8A)?
GIVEN facility IS A `Temporary facility` @desc Which kind of temporary facility the carrier installed
      `it has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the carrier has removed the facility
      `days so far` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting days from the day the maintenance or replacement was completed, the event (or last event) ended, or the emergency need ended: on which day was the facility removed, or, if it has not been, how many days have passed until today
GIVETH A `Removal status`
DECIDE `Was the temporary facility removed in time` IS
    BRANCH
        IF facility EQUALS `a temporary tower for a high-demand holiday period (cl 6(5)(f))`
        THEN `not covered: cl 8A sets no removal deadline for a holiday-period tower; see the calendar-year limit in cl 8C`
        IF `the rule ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE `cl 8A -- the carrier must remove the temporary facility within 28 days` 0 `what happened`)
        THEN `in time: the carrier removed the temporary facility within 28 days (cl 8A)`
        IF `it has been removed` OR `days so far` GREATER THAN `the days to remove a temporary facility`
        THEN `late: the carrier did not remove the temporary facility within 28 days (cl 8A)`
        OTHERWISE `not yet late: the 28 days have not run out (cl 8A)`
    WHERE
        `what happened` MEANS
            IF `it has been removed`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `remove the temporary facility` `days so far`)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL `days so far`)

-- cl 8B(1): event towers (cl 6(5)(d), (e)): "the total number of days in a calendar year on which those facilities remain at
-- that place does not exceed 183." cl 8C(1): holiday towers (cl 6(5)(f)): "does not exceed 90."
`the most days in a calendar year for event towers` MEANS 183
`the most days in a calendar year for holiday towers` MEANS 90

@export Have temporary event or holiday towers stayed at this place for more days this calendar year than the Act allows (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 8B, 8C)? No answer means no calendar-year limit applies to that kind of facility.
GIVEN facility IS A `Temporary facility` @desc Which kind of temporary facility the carrier installed
      `days at the place this calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days in this calendar year have such temporary facilities remained at that place (counting every day on which any of them was there)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have temporary towers stayed beyond the calendar-year limit` IS
    CONSIDER facility
    WHEN `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` THEN JUST (`days at the place this calendar year` GREATER THAN `the most days in a calendar year for event towers`)
    WHEN `a temporary tower for a series of events at a venue (cl 6(5)(e))` THEN JUST (`days at the place this calendar year` GREATER THAN `the most days in a calendar year for event towers`)
    WHEN `a temporary tower for a high-demand holiday period (cl 6(5)(f))` THEN JUST (`days at the place this calendar year` GREATER THAN `the most days in a calendar year for holiday towers`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `cl 9, 9A -- by when must the carrier start restoring my land`

-- cl 9(1): "the carrier must take all reasonable steps to ensure that the land is restored to a condition that is similar to
-- its condition before the activity began." (2): "... that the restoration begins within 10 business days after the
-- completion of the first-mentioned activity." (3): "The rule in subclause (2) does not apply if the carrier agrees with: (a)
-- the owner of the land; and (b) if the land is occupied by a person other than the owner--the occupier; to commence
-- restoration at a time after the end of that period of 10 business days." cl 9A(3)-(5): the same, 10 business days after
-- the removal of a temporary facility.
`the business days to begin restoration` MEANS 10

GIVEN `the owner agreed a later start` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land is occupied by someone other than the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupier agreed a later start` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreed start in business days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the restoration start period` IS
    IF      `the owner agreed a later start`
        AND (    (NOT `the land is occupied by someone other than the owner`)
             OR  `the occupier agreed a later start`)
        AND `the agreed start in business days` GREATER THAN `the business days to begin restoration`
    THEN `the agreed start in business days`
    ELSE `the business days to begin restoration`

@export How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land after it finishes the work, or after it removes a temporary facility (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 9, 9A)?
GIVEN `the owner agreed a later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner of the land agreed with the carrier that restoration may begin later than 10 business days after the work (or the removal)
      `the land is occupied by someone other than the owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone other than the owner occupies the land (for example a tenant)
      `the occupier agreed a later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where someone other than the owner occupies the land: whether that occupier also agreed to the later start
      `the agreed start in business days` IS A NUMBER @desc The later start agreed, as a number of business days after the work was completed (or the facility removed); enter 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land` IS
    `the restoration start period` `the owner agreed a later start` `the land is occupied by someone other than the owner` `the occupier agreed a later start` `the agreed start in business days`

-- The restoration duty as a rule, in business days from completion of the work (cl 9) or removal of the facility (cl 9A).
-- The text's duty is to "take all reasonable steps to ensure" that restoration begins in time; the rule tracks the
-- beginning itself, so a breach here is where the reasonable-steps question starts, not where it ends (NOTES.md, finding 5).
GIVEN `the period to begin` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land party` `Land act`
DECIDE `cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4) -- the carrier must begin restoring my land in time` IS
    PARTY `the carrier`
    MUST  `begin restoring my land`
    WITHIN `the period to begin`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the carrier` BECAUSE "cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4): the carrier must take all reasonable steps to ensure that restoration begins within 10 business days, or the later time agreed with the owner and any occupier"

DECLARE `Restoration status` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the carrier began restoring my land within the period (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
    `late: the carrier did not begin restoring my land within the period, so it must show it took all reasonable steps to ensure that it did (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
    `not yet late: the period for beginning restoration has not run out (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`

@export Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time after finishing its work, or after removing a temporary facility (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 9, 9A)?
GIVEN `the owner agreed a later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner of the land agreed with the carrier that restoration may begin later than 10 business days after the work (or the removal)
      `the land is occupied by someone other than the owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone other than the owner occupies the land (for example a tenant)
      `the occupier agreed a later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where someone other than the owner occupies the land: whether that occupier also agreed to the later start
      `the agreed start in business days` IS A NUMBER @desc The later start agreed, as a number of business days after the work was completed (or the facility removed); enter 0 if none
      `restoration has begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the carrier has begun restoring the land
      `business days so far` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting business days from the day the work was completed (or the facility removed): on which business day did restoration begin, or, if it has not begun, how many business days have passed until today
GIVETH A `Restoration status`
DECIDE `Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the rule ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4) -- the carrier must begin restoring my land in time` `the period`) 0 `what happened`)
        THEN `in time: the carrier began restoring my land within the period (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
        IF `restoration has begun` OR `business days so far` GREATER THAN `the period`
        THEN `late: the carrier did not begin restoring my land within the period, so it must show it took all reasonable steps to ensure that it did (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
        OTHERWISE `not yet late: the period for beginning restoration has not run out (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
    WHERE
        `the period` MEANS `the restoration start period` `the owner agreed a later start` `the land is occupied by someone other than the owner` `the occupier agreed a later start` `the agreed start in business days`
        `what happened` MEANS
            IF `restoration has begun`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `begin restoring my land` `business days so far`)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL `business days so far`)

§§ `cl 42, 43, 46(7) -- can I claim compensation for loss or damage the carrier caused`

-- cl 42(1): "If a person suffers financial loss or damage because of anything done by a carrier under Division 2, 3 or 4 in
-- relation to: (a) any property owned by the person; or (b) any property in which the person has an interest; there is
-- payable to the person by the carrier such reasonable amount of compensation: (c) as is agreed between them; or (d) failing
-- agreement--as is determined by a court of competent jurisdiction." (2): it "includes, without limitation, compensation in
-- relation to: (a) damage of a temporary character as well as of a permanent character; and (b) the taking of sand, soil,
-- stone, gravel, timber, water and other things." cl 43: the carrier's powers extend to its employees, contractors and
-- contractors' employees, so what they do under Division 2, 3 or 4 is done "by a carrier" here. cl 46(7): an ACMA limit on
-- tort damages "does not apply to a cause of action under clause 42".
DECLARE `Compensation answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the carrier must pay me a reasonable amount of compensation, as agreed between us or, failing agreement, as a court decides; it covers temporary as well as permanent damage and the taking of sand, soil, stone, gravel, timber, water and other things, and no ACMA limit on tort damages applies to it (cl 42(1), (2), 46(7))`
    `no compensation under cl 42: I have not suffered financial loss or damage (cl 42(1))`
    `no compensation under cl 42: the loss or damage was not caused by anything the carrier, its employees or contractors did under Division 2, 3 or 4 (cl 42(1), 43)`
    `no compensation under cl 42: the loss or damage is not in relation to property I own or have an interest in (cl 42(1)(a), (b))`

@export Can I claim compensation from a carrier for financial loss or damage caused by its inspection, installation or maintenance work on land (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 42)?
GIVEN `I suffered financial loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have suffered financial loss or damage (temporary damage counts, as does the taking of sand, soil, stone, gravel, timber, water or other things)
      activity IS A `Carrier activity` @desc What caused it: the carrier's inspecting or surveying (Division 2), installing a facility (Division 3), maintaining a facility (Division 4), or something not done under those Divisions
      `the carrier or its people caused it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loss or damage was because of something done by the carrier, its employee, a contractor acting for it, or the contractor's employee
      `I own the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the property that was damaged or affected (land, buildings, crops, stock, goods)
      `I have an interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an interest in that property without owning it (for example as a lessee or mortgagee)
GIVETH A `Compensation answer`
DECIDE `Can I claim compensation for loss or damage from the carrier` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `I suffered financial loss or damage`)
        THEN `no compensation under cl 42: I have not suffered financial loss or damage (cl 42(1))`
        IF (NOT (`it is an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4` activity)) OR (NOT `the carrier or its people caused it`)
        THEN `no compensation under cl 42: the loss or damage was not caused by anything the carrier, its employees or contractors did under Division 2, 3 or 4 (cl 42(1), 43)`
        IF (NOT `I own the property`) AND (NOT `I have an interest in the property`)
        THEN `no compensation under cl 42: the loss or damage is not in relation to property I own or have an interest in (cl 42(1)(a), (b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the carrier must pay me a reasonable amount of compensation, as agreed between us or, failing agreement, as a court decides; it covers temporary as well as permanent damage and the taking of sand, soil, stone, gravel, timber, water and other things, and no ACMA limit on tort damages applies to it (cl 42(1), (2), 46(7))`

-- cl 42(3): "court of competent jurisdiction, in relation to property, means: (a) the Federal Court; or (b) the Supreme Court
-- of the State or Territory in which the property is situated or was situated at the time of the relevant loss or damage;
-- or (c) an inferior court that has jurisdiction: (i) for the recovery of debts up to an amount not less than the amount of
-- compensation claimed by the person; and (ii) in relation to the locality in which the property, or part of the property,
-- is situated or was situated ..." The inferior court's debt limit is set by State or Territory law: an input.
DECLARE `Courts for my claim` IS ONE OF
    `the Federal Court, the Supreme Court of the State or Territory where the property is, or a local inferior court whose debt limit is at least my claim (cl 42(3))`
    `the Federal Court or the Supreme Court of the State or Territory where the property is; my claim is above the local inferior court's debt limit (cl 42(3))`

@export If the carrier and I cannot agree on compensation, which courts can decide it (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 42(1)(d), (3))?
GIVEN `the compensation I claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of compensation you claim, in dollars
      `the local inferior court's debt limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The most a County, District, Local or Magistrates Court for the locality where the property is can award in a debt claim, in dollars; enter 0 if no such court has jurisdiction there
GIVETH A `Courts for my claim`
DECIDE `Which courts can decide my compensation` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the local inferior court's debt limit` AT LEAST `the compensation I claim`
        THEN `the Federal Court, the Supreme Court of the State or Territory where the property is, or a local inferior court whose debt limit is at least my claim (cl 42(3))`
        OTHERWISE `the Federal Court or the Supreme Court of the State or Territory where the property is; my claim is above the local inferior court's debt limit (cl 42(3))`

§§ `cl 62, 63; s 591 -- if my property is in effect acquired` -- arises only where a court would find an acquisition of property

-- cl 62(1): "If: (a) either of the following would result in an acquisition of property from a person: (i) anything done by a
-- carrier under, or because of, this Schedule; (ii) the existence of rights conferred on a carrier under, or because of, this
-- Schedule in relation to a building, structure or facility owned or operated by the carrier; and (b) the acquisition of
-- property would not be valid, apart from this clause, because a particular person had not been compensated; the carrier
-- must pay that person: (c) a reasonable amount of compensation agreed on between the person and the carrier; or (d)
-- failing agreement--a reasonable amount of compensation determined by a court of competent jurisdiction." (2): compensation
-- already obtained by agreement, or recovered in another proceeding, for the same event "must be taken into account". (3):
-- "This clause does not limit the operation of clause 42." cl 63: Part 3 applies to things done, and rights conferred, after
-- the commencement of Schedule 2 to the Telecommunications and Other Legislation Amendment (Protection of Submarine Cables
-- and Other Measures) Act 2005 (a date not stated in the deposit: asked as a fact).
-- s 591(1): "If: (a) apart from this section, the operation of this Act would result in the acquisition of property from a
-- person otherwise than on just terms; and (b) the acquisition would be invalid because of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the
-- Constitution; the Commonwealth is liable to pay compensation of a reasonable amount to the person in respect of the
-- acquisition." (2): failing agreement, "proceedings in the Federal Court".
DECLARE `Acquisition answer` IS ONE OF
    `the carrier must pay me a reasonable amount of compensation, agreed or, failing agreement, decided by a court; anything I already obtained or recovered for the same event is taken into account, and my cl 42 claim is not limited (cl 62)`
    `the Commonwealth is liable to pay me a reasonable amount of compensation; failing agreement I may sue it in the Federal Court (s 591)`
    `no compensation under cl 62 or s 591: there is no acquisition of my property that would be invalid without compensation (cl 62(1), s 591(1))`

@export If a carrier's work or rights under Schedule 3, or the Act otherwise, would in effect acquire my property, who must compensate me (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 62, 63; s 591)?
GIVEN `there would be an acquisition of my property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find that the work or rights result in an acquisition of property from you, in the sense of the Constitution, s 51(xxxi)
      `it would be invalid unless I am compensated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that acquisition would be invalid because you had not been compensated (not on just terms)
      `it comes from the carrier under Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it comes from something the carrier did under or because of Schedule 3, or from rights Schedule 3 gives the carrier over its building, structure or facility
      `it happened after the 2005 amendments began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the thing was done, or the rights conferred, after Schedule 2 to the Telecommunications and Other Legislation Amendment (Protection of Submarine Cables and Other Measures) Act 2005 commenced
GIVETH A `Acquisition answer`
DECIDE `Who must compensate me for an acquisition of my property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `there would be an acquisition of my property`) OR (NOT `it would be invalid unless I am compensated`)
        THEN `no compensation under cl 62 or s 591: there is no acquisition of my property that would be invalid without compensation (cl 62(1), s 591(1))`
        IF `it comes from the carrier under Schedule 3` AND `it happened after the 2005 amendments began`
        THEN `the carrier must pay me a reasonable amount of compensation, agreed or, failing agreement, decided by a court; anything I already obtained or recovered for the same event is taken into account, and my cl 42 claim is not limited (cl 62)`
        OTHERWISE `the Commonwealth is liable to pay me a reasonable amount of compensation; failing agreement I may sue it in the Federal Court (s 591)`

§§ `cl 47, 53 -- whose is the facility on my land, and must I pay if I subdivide`

-- cl 47: "Unless the circumstances indicate otherwise, a facility, or a part of a facility, that is supplied, installed,
-- maintained or operated by a carrier remains the property of its owner: (a) in any case--whether or not it has become
-- (either in whole or in part), a fixture; ..."
DECLARE `Facility ownership` IS ONE OF
    `not mine: the facility remains the property of its owner even if it has become a fixture on my land (cl 47(a))`
    `cl 47 does not settle it: the circumstances indicate otherwise, so ownership turns on those circumstances (cl 47)`

@export Does a carrier's facility on my land (a cable, pit or tower) become my property because it is fixed to the land (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 47)?
GIVEN `the circumstances indicate otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the circumstances indicate that the facility does not remain its owner's property (for example, an agreement transferring it to you)
GIVETH A `Facility ownership`
DECIDE `Is the carrier's facility on my land mine` IS
    IF `the circumstances indicate otherwise`
    THEN `cl 47 does not settle it: the circumstances indicate otherwise, so ownership turns on those circumstances (cl 47)`
    ELSE `not mine: the facility remains the property of its owner even if it has become a fixture on my land (cl 47(a))`

-- cl 53: "If: (a) it becomes necessary, in the opinion of a carrier, because of the subdivision of any land, to remove, or
-- alter the position of, a facility on, over or under the land; and (b) the carrier incurs costs in connection with anything
-- reasonably done in connection with the removal or alteration; the person who subdivided the land is liable to pay to the
-- carrier so much of those costs as is reasonable, and that amount may be recovered in a court of competent jurisdiction as a
-- debt due to the carrier." The carrier's opinion and what is reasonable are inputs.
DECLARE `Subdivision liability` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must pay the carrier so much of its costs as is reasonable, and it may recover that amount from me in court as a debt (cl 53)`
    `no: cl 53 makes only the person who subdivided the land liable`
    `no: the carrier is not of the opinion that the subdivision made the removal or alteration necessary (cl 53(a))`
    `no: the carrier has incurred no costs in anything reasonably done for the removal or alteration (cl 53(b))`

@export If I subdivide my land and the carrier moves or alters its facility because of it, must I pay the carrier's costs (Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3, cl 53)?
GIVEN `I subdivided the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who subdivided the land
      `the carrier considers the subdivision made it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the carrier is of the opinion that the subdivision made it necessary to remove or move a facility on, over or under the land
      `the carrier incurred costs in reasonable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the carrier incurred costs in anything reasonably done to remove or move the facility
GIVETH A `Subdivision liability`
DECIDE `Must I pay for moving the facility because I subdivided` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `I subdivided the land`)
        THEN `no: cl 53 makes only the person who subdivided the land liable`
        IF (NOT `the carrier considers the subdivision made it necessary`)
        THEN `no: the carrier is not of the opinion that the subdivision made the removal or alteration necessary (cl 53(a))`
        IF (NOT `the carrier incurred costs in reasonable work`)
        THEN `no: the carrier has incurred no costs in anything reasonably done for the removal or alteration (cl 53(b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: I must pay the carrier so much of its costs as is reasonable, and it may recover that amount from me in court as a debt (cl 53)`
